>>
endobj
1006 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 515 0 R
/E (Let no seed I planted in faith go without a harvest. I believe Your Word when it says in Galatians 6:9 that in due season I shall reap if I faint not. I have not fainted. I am still standing. I am still sowing. I am still trusting. And I ask You to release the due season harvest for every area of seed I have planted. Let financial seeds produce financial harvests. Let seeds of service produce seasons of being served. Let seeds of generosity produce oceans of generosity returned to me. Let what goes out from me in faith come back to me in multiplication.)
/Pg 75 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
1007 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 515 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 75 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
1008 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 515 0 R
/E (Let me keep sowing even while I wait for the harvest on what I have already planted. Let me be a consistent, faithful, generous sower who never grows tired of planting because I never lose confidence in the God who makes things grow. In Jesus' name, Amen.)
/Pg 75 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
1009 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 516 0 R
/T (Blessing My Rest)
/E (Blessing My Rest)
/Pg 76 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
1010 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 516 0 R
/E (Father, in a culture that glorifies overwork and celebrates burnout as if it were a badge of honor, I come before You today and ask for the countercultural blessing of genuine rest. Not laziness. Not avoidance. Not the kind of rest that comes from giving up. But the deep, restorative, Sabbath rest of someone who has worked faithfully, planted strategically, and now trusts You enough to step back and let Your work continue while theirs pauses.)
/Pg 76 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
1011 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 516 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 76 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
1012 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 516 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 76 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
1013 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 516 0 R
/E (And let my rest be an act of faith. Let stepping away from the building be my way of saying, "God, I trust You to keep working even when I stop." Let my rest demonstrate a confidence in Your provision that does not require my constant striving to maintain. In Jesus' name, Amen.)
/Pg 76 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
